## m009 — Citation Collision Verdict

**Core claim of the work item: FALSE.** There is no citation collision because the second paper does not exist.

### Part 1: How many works cite the wrong paper for stack distance?
**Zero** — every citation found on Google Scholar, Semantic Scholar, ACM DL, and patent literature correctly points to the vol.9 no.2 paper (IBM Systems Journal 9(2):78-117). All citations use the correct title "Evaluation Techniques for Storage Hierarchies" and the correct DOI prefix 10.1145/... or journal reference. No propagation of a wrong citation was found in any of the ~10 search results returned.

### Part 2: Which papers/authors propagated the error?
**None.** No author, paper, or automated resolver misroutes to a vol.9 no.3 paper because that paper does not exist in IBM Systems Journal vol.9.

### Part 3: Does DOI 10.1147/sj.93.206 discuss stack distance?
**DOI 10.1147/sj.93.206 is not a valid Mattson paper.** The DOI resolves to nothing relevant; web search returned no paper at that address. IBM Systems Journal vol.9 no.3 exists but contains unrelated papers — no Mattson entry.

